+# JSRF v19 Windows run — retail game main returns after negative startup status
+
+Date: 2026-09-07
+
+## Observed behavior
+
+The v19 Windows run no longer reaches either of the previous watchdog stalls.
+The JSRF-specific NV2A fence mirror is registered, the retail D3D wait at
+`0x00191440` reaches its post-wait block at `0x001914FC`, and the process later
+exits through `HalReturnToFirmware(2)` with launch-data words `1, 0, 1, 0`.
+The host exits with code 0 because this is a title-requested reboot, not a host
+crash.
+
+## Retail control flow
+
+The XBE entry point (`0x00148023`) creates the main title thread.  The successful
+Windows trace shows that thread creation succeeds, so the entry-point failure
+path at `0x0014806F` is not the observed reboot.
+
+The title-thread wrapper at `0x00147FB4` calls the retail game main at
+`0x0006F9E0`.  When that function returns, the wrapper executes:
+
+- `push 0`
+- `push 1`
+- `push 1`
+- `call 0x0014ADA3`
+
+`0x0014ADA3` builds a zeroed launch-data block whose first four dwords are
+`arg1, 0, arg2, arg3`, then calls the `XLaunchNewImage`-style helper at
+`0x00147532`.  That helper constructs the launch-data page and calls
+`HalReturnToFirmware(2)`.  Therefore the v19 launch data `1, 0, 1, 0` matches the
+normal "game main returned" path at `0x00148019`.
+
+## Why retail game main returns
+
+`0x0006F9E0` has a compact application lifetime:
+
+1. allocate and construct the main application object (`0x00012210`);
+2. call setup method `0x00012C10`;
+3. call run method `0x00013F80`;
+4. destroy the object and return 0.
+
+The constructor stores the return value of `sub_0005F350` at object offset
+`+0x10`.  Both setup and run test that same field.  `0x00012C10` skips setup if
+it is negative, while `0x00013F80` returns `-1` immediately if it is negative.
+If the value is non-negative, `0x00013F80` enters the title's persistent loop.
+
+So the next concrete question is not why XAPI reboots: the retail game main has
+already returned.  The question is which subsystem inside `sub_0005F350`
+produces the negative startup status stored at `+0x10`.
+
+## v20 diagnostic scope
+
+v20 adds trace-only coverage for the retail game-main/startup chain and the
+direct status-producing calls inside `sub_0005F350`.  No guest state is changed.
+The trace includes:
+
+- `0x0006F9E0` — retail game main
+- `0x00012210` — main application constructor
+- `0x0005F350` — startup status producer
+- `0x00012C10` — setup status check
+- `0x00013F80` — run-loop status check
+- `0x0014CAA0`, `0x001BB690`, `0x0014CAF0`, `0x001BB750`
+- `0x0005F2C0`, `0x0005F250`, `0x00156DF0`
+- `0x001680D0`, `0x00116EC0`
+- `0x0014ADA3`, `0x00147532` — reboot path confirmation
+
+This is deliberately diagnostic only.  The repeated `NtFreeVirtualMemory`
+failures and any D3D/audio return value are not changed until the trace proves
+which one is causal.
